# AdoboFlix environment configuration
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values:
#   cp .env.example .env

# PostgreSQL connection string. Required ONLY by the postgres-direct source.
# adobotv-http and file read no database at all, and the server does not open a
# connection for them — so this key can stay unset for those two sources.
ADOBOFLIX_PG_URL=postgres://user:password@127.0.0.1:5432/yourdb?sslmode=disable

# Fallback alias (used if ADOBOFLIX_PG_URL is not set)
# MPDUMPY_PG_URL=postgres://user:password@127.0.0.1:5432/yourdb?sslmode=disable

# Content source adapter. OPTIONAL — an OVERRIDE. When set it pins the source
# and wins; when unset the server uses the mode chosen in the UI (below), and
# with neither it boots with no source and offers the two choices. Available
# values:
#   adobotv-http     — the real subscriber path ("Login to AdoboTV"): talks to
#                      AdoboTV over HTTP with your playlist code, no database.
#   file             — the no-account path ("Import Local Playlist"): a local
#                      playlist in JSON or M3U, no database.
#   postgres-direct  — development test harness that reads the AdoboTV database
#                      directly. It bypasses entitlement, device authorisation and
#                      AdoboTV's analytics, and must never be used by end users.
#                      This is the ONLY way to select it: it is not a UI choice.
# Uncomment the line below only if you are deliberately running the harness.
# See docs/source-adapters.md.
# ADOBOFLIX_SOURCE=postgres-direct

# Optional. Where the source mode chosen in the UI ("Login to AdoboTV" or
# "Import Local Playlist") is remembered. Defaults to .adoboflix/source-mode
# (gitignored). ADOBOFLIX_SOURCE above overrides it.
# ADOBOFLIX_SOURCE_MODE_FILE=.adoboflix/source-mode

# ── adobotv-http (ADOBOFLIX_SOURCE=adobotv-http) ──────────────────────────────
# The real subscriber path. ADOBOFLIX_ADOBOTV_BASE_URL is required; the server
# fails fast and names the missing key rather than booting half-configured.
# ADOBOFLIX_ADOBOTV_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080

# The subscriber's playlist code. OPTIONAL now that the UI can enter one: the
# server boots without a code, and the code-entry screen (POST
# /api/v1/source/playlist-code) saves one to ADOBOFLIX_PLAYLIST_CODE_FILE.
#
# PRECEDENCE: a code entered in the UI and saved to the file WINS over this
# variable; this variable is the fallback used only when no code has been
# stored. A code entered in the UI is the user's most recent explicit
# instruction, and a stale value here silently overriding it would make the UI
# look broken. Delete the stored code (the UI's "clear" action, or DELETE
# /api/v1/source/playlist-code) to fall back to this variable again.
# ADOBOFLIX_ADOBOTV_PLAYLIST_CODE=your-playlist-code

# Optional. Where the UI-entered playlist code is stored. Defaults to
# .adoboflix/playlist-code (gitignored). The file is written mode 0600 and is
# the credential itself, so keep it off any shared filesystem and out of version
# control.
# ADOBOFLIX_PLAYLIST_CODE_FILE=.adoboflix/playlist-code

# Optional. Sent upstream as the User-Agent. The default begins with "AdoboFlix",
# which AdoboTV's allowlist accepts and which makes this client identifiable in
# the operator's audit logs.
# ADOBOFLIX_ADOBOTV_USER_AGENT=AdoboFlix/1.0 (+https://github.com/jmvbambico/adoboflix)
# Optional. How long the playlist envelope and VOD library are cached in memory.
# Defaults to 5m, matching AdoboTV's own playlist cache. Do not lower it below
# that: AdoboTV caches for 5 minutes, so a shorter TTL only adds latency.
# ADOBOFLIX_ADOBOTV_CACHE_TTL=5m

# ── file (the "Import Local Playlist" path) ───────────────────────────────────
# A local playlist for a user with no AdoboTV account. Either import one through
# the UI (POST /api/v1/source/playlist-file), which stores it below and selects
# this mode, or point ADOBOFLIX_FILE_PATH at a file you already have.
#
# ADOBOFLIX_FILE_PATH: a path to a playlist on disk. Used only when nothing has
# been imported; an imported playlist wins. The file is read once when the mode
# opens, never written, and the database is not touched by this source at all.
# Formats: the JSON envelope documented in docs/source-adapters.md (a direct
# serialisation of the internal library models), or M3U/M3U8. The parser is
# chosen by extension.
# ADOBOFLIX_FILE_PATH=/absolute/path/to/playlist.json

# Optional. Where a playlist imported through the UI is stored. Defaults to
# .adoboflix/playlist (gitignored); the extension (.json or .m3u) is added from
# the detected format. Written mode 0600.
# ADOBOFLIX_PLAYLIST_FILE=.adoboflix/playlist

# Backend bind address (default: 127.0.0.1)
# Loopback by default: /api/v1/proxy is an unauthenticated fetcher and
# /api/v1/resolve returns the upstream CDN URL, so binding 0.0.0.0 offers both
# to the whole LAN. Set it only when you mean to expose AdoboFlix.
# SERVER_HOST=127.0.0.1
# SERVER_PORT=5656

# Vite dev server proxy target (default: http://127.0.0.1:5656)
# ADOBOFLIX_API=http://127.0.0.1:5656
